# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy. The page boots Pyodide (Python via
# WebAssembly) by injecting a <script> from cdn.jsdelivr.net, falling back to
# unpkg.com, and Pyodide then fetches its own .wasm and package files at
# runtime. A CSP tight enough to be worth having would need, at minimum:
#
#   script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob:
#              https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com;
#   connect-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com;
#   worker-src blob:;
#
# That is easy to get subtly wrong, and when it is wrong the failure is silent:
# the page still renders and only the interactive demo dies. Add it once someone
# can load the page and actually run the Python panel to confirm it survives.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
